concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-12 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "101(12) 2, 102.2, 102.4, 103.1 and 103.2 and Division 119 of the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-101-ss-12 ;
    values:originalText "(12) The Minister may determine in writing that a notice under paragraph (10)(a) should not be given to a person if the Minister is satisfied that giving the notice could prejudice the security, defence or international relations of Australia, or Australian law enforcement operations. The Minister must consider whether to revoke such a determination:  (a) no later than 6 months after making it; and  (b) at least every 6 months thereafter until 5 years have passed since the determination was made. Minister’s power to rescind notice and exempt person" ;
    skos:definition "(12) The Minister may determine in writing that a notice under paragraph (10)(a) should not be given to a person if the Minister is satisfied that giving the notice could prejudice the security, defence or international relations of Australia, or Australian law enforcement operations. The Minister must consider whether to revoke such a determination:  (a) no later than 6 months after making it; and  (b) at least every 6 months thereafter until 5 years have passed since the determination was made. Minister’s power to rescind notice and exempt person"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b6dfaf3c7abe7a70b807a81ba5d301e5c70882f1fbc6423ce0bd5b73042cfc48" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101 ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Minister may determine that a notice should not be given to a person under certain circumstances." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
