concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-15 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "101(15) 2, 102.2, 102.4, 103.1 and 103.2 and Division 119 of the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-101-ss-15 ;
    values:originalText "(15) The Minister does not have a duty to consider whether to exercise the power under subsection (14) in respect of any person, whether the Minister is requested to do so by the person who has renounced his or her citizenship under this section, or by any other person, or in any other circumstances." ;
    skos:definition "(15) The Minister does not have a duty to consider whether to exercise the power under subsection (14) in respect of any person, whether the Minister is requested to do so by the person who has renounced his or her citizenship under this section, or by any other person, or in any other circumstances."@en ;
