concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101-ss-17 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "101(17) 2, 102.2, 102.4, 103.1 and 103.2 and Division 119 of the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-101-ss-17 ;
    values:originalText "(17) If the Minister decides to consider whether to exercise the power in subsection (14), then, in that consideration, the Minister must have regard to the following:  (a) the severity of the matters that were the basis for any notice given in respect of the person under subsection (10), or of matters that would have been the basis for giving a notice in ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166  Main amendments  Schedule 1  No. 166, 2015 Australian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015  respect of the person under paragraph (10)(a), but for the operation of subsection (12);  (b) the degree of threat posed by the person to the Australian community;  (c) the age of the person;  (d) if the person is aged under 18—the best interests of the child as a primary consideration;  (e) whether the person is being or is likely to be prosecuted in relation to matters referred to in paragraph (a);  (f) the person’s connection to the other country of which the person is a national or citizen and the availability of the rights of citizenship of that country to the person;  (g) Australia’s international relations;  (h) any other matters of public interest." ;
    skos:definition "(17) If the Minister decides to consider whether to exercise the power in subsection (14), then, in that consideration, the Minister must have regard to the following:  (a) the severity of the matters that were the basis for any notice given in respect of the person under subsection (10), or of matters that would have been the basis for giving a notice in ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166  Main amendments  Schedule 1  No. 166, 2015 Australian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015  respect of the person under paragraph (10)(a), but for the operation of subsection (12);  (b) the degree of threat posed by the person to the Australian community;  (c) the age of the person;  (d) if the person is aged under 18—the best interests of the child as a primary consideration;  (e) whether the person is being or is likely to be prosecuted in relation to matters referred to in paragraph (a);  (f) the person’s connection to the other country of which the person is a national or citizen and the availability of the rights of citizenship of that country to the person;  (g) Australia’s international relations;  (h) any other matters of public interest."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "828f5cbf4fc5090de3760c05f179236f72a0f025fe63bac57008bbc387932fce" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-101 ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Minister must consider certain factors when deciding whether to exercise power." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015.pdf> ;
