doc:sch-1-sec-35-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "35(4) Service outside Australia in armed forces of an enemy country or" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) For the purposes of subparagraph (1)(b)(ii) and without limitation, a person is not in the service of a declared terrorist organisation to the extent that:  (a) the person’s actions are unintentional; or  (b) the person is acting under duress or force; or  (c) the person is providing neutral and independent humanitarian assistance. Minister to give notice" ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "35(5) Service outside Australia in armed forces of an enemy country or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-35-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) If the Minister becomes aware of conduct because of which a person has, under this section, ceased to be an Australian citizen, the Minister:  (a) must give, or make reasonable attempts to give, written notice to that effect to the person:  (i) as soon as practicable; or  (ii) if the Minister makes a determination under subsection (7)—as soon as practicable after the Minister revokes the determination (if the Minister does so); and  (b) may give notice to that effect to such other persons and at such time as the Minister considers appropriate. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166  Schedule 1  Main amendments  Australian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015 No. 166, 2015  Note: A person may seek review of the basis on which a notice under this subsection was given in the High Court of Australia under section 75 of the Constitution, or in the Federal Court of Australia under section 39B of the Judiciary Act 1903." ;
    skos:definition "(5) If the Minister becomes aware of conduct because of which a person has, under this section, ceased to be an Australian citizen, the Minister:  (a) must give, or make reasonable attempts to give, written notice to that effect to the person:  (i) as soon as practicable; or  (ii) if the Minister makes a determination under subsection (7)—as soon as practicable after the Minister revokes the determination (if the Minister does so); and  (b) may give notice to that effect to such other persons and at such time as the Minister considers appropriate. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166  Schedule 1  Main amendments  Australian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015 No. 166, 2015  Note: A person may seek review of the basis on which a notice under this subsection was given in the High Court of Australia under section 75 of the Constitution, or in the Federal Court of Australia under section 39B of the Judiciary Act 1903."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "81429bee585f674d681da997771f9c7c607916757aab58a0bc64146c4f546ca9" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35 ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Must give written notice to a person who has ceased to be an Australian citizen." ;
    dc:description "written notice" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
