doc:sch-1-sec-35-ss-12 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "35(12) Service outside Australia in armed forces of an enemy country or" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(12) If the Minister decides to consider whether to exercise the power in subsection (9), then, in that consideration, the Minister must have regard to the following:  (a) the severity of the matters that were the basis for any notice given in respect of the person under subsection (5), or of matters that would have been the basis for giving a notice in respect of the person under paragraph (5)(a), but for the operation of subsection (7);  (b) the degree of threat posed by the person to the Australian community;  (c) the age of the person;  (d) if the person is aged under 18—the best interests of the child as a primary consideration;  (e) whether the person is being or is likely to be prosecuted in relation to matters referred to in paragraph (a);  (f) the person’s connection to the other country of which the person is a national or citizen and the availability of the rights of citizenship of that country to the person;  (g) Australia’s international relations;  (h) any other matters of public interest." ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35-ss-13 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "35(13) Service outside Australia in armed forces of an enemy country or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-35-ss-13 ;
    values:originalText "(13) If the Minister makes a determination under subsection (9), the Minister must cause to be laid before each House of the Parliament, within 15 sitting days of that House after the Minister makes the determination, a statement that:  (a) sets out the determination; and  (b) sets out the reasons for the determination, referring in particular to the Minister’s reasons in relation to the matters set out in subsection (12)." ;
    skos:definition "(13) If the Minister makes a determination under subsection (9), the Minister must cause to be laid before each House of the Parliament, within 15 sitting days of that House after the Minister makes the determination, a statement that:  (a) sets out the determination; and  (b) sets out the reasons for the determination, referring in particular to the Minister’s reasons in relation to the matters set out in subsection (12)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ffe979ba1b1c62aba7a33960c408b72106e38b7c572f7ef951f5de520e4e11aa" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35 ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Minister must provide statement to Parliament within 15 days of determination." ;
    dc:description "true" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
