concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "35A(7) Conviction for terrorism offences and certain other offences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-35a-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) The Minister may determine in writing that a notice under paragraph (5)(a) should not be given to a person if the Minister is satisfied that giving the notice could prejudice the security, defence or international relations of Australia, or Australian law enforcement operations. The Minister must consider whether to revoke the determination:  (a) no later than 6 months after making it; and  (b) at least every 6 months thereafter until 5 years have passed since the determination was made. Minister must revoke determination if conviction overturned" ;
    skos:definition "(7) The Minister may determine in writing that a notice under paragraph (5)(a) should not be given to a person if the Minister is satisfied that giving the notice could prejudice the security, defence or international relations of Australia, or Australian law enforcement operations. The Minister must consider whether to revoke the determination:  (a) no later than 6 months after making it; and  (b) at least every 6 months thereafter until 5 years have passed since the determination was made. Minister must revoke determination if conviction overturned"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "52354be297a4025080542a0cc5b3b8d09d354a89b8df07c85426ec175f9bc670" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Notice not to be given under certain circumstances" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
