doc:sch-1-sec-35a-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "35A(2) Conviction for terrorism offences and certain other offences" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A notice that is given to a person under paragraph 35A(5)(a) must:  (a) state that the Minister has determined under section 35A that the person has ceased to be an Australian citizen; and  (b) include the reasons for the decision to make the determination." ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "35A(3) Conviction for terrorism offences and certain other offences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-35a-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) However, a notice given to a person under paragraph 33AA(10)(a), 35(5)(a) or 35A(5)(a) must not contain information, or content of a document, if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166  Schedule 1  Main amendments  Australian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015 No. 166, 2015  (a) the information or content includes any operationally sensitive information (within the meaning of the Independent National Security Legislation Monitor Act 2010); or  (b) the disclosure of the information or content would or might prejudice:  (i) the security, defence or international relations of Australia; or  (ii) the performance by a law enforcement or security agency (within the meaning of the Independent National Security Legislation Monitor Act 2010) of its functions; or  (c) the disclosure of the information or content would or might endanger a person’s safety; or  (d) the disclosure of the information or content would be likely to be contrary to the public interest for any other reason." ;
    skos:definition "(3) However, a notice given to a person under paragraph 33AA(10)(a), 35(5)(a) or 35A(5)(a) must not contain information, or content of a document, if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00166  Schedule 1  Main amendments  Australian Citizenship Amendment (Allegiance to Australia) Act 2015 No. 166, 2015  (a) the information or content includes any operationally sensitive information (within the meaning of the Independent National Security Legislation Monitor Act 2010); or  (b) the disclosure of the information or content would or might prejudice:  (i) the security, defence or international relations of Australia; or  (ii) the performance by a law enforcement or security agency (within the meaning of the Independent National Security Legislation Monitor Act 2010) of its functions; or  (c) the disclosure of the information or content would or might endanger a person’s safety; or  (d) the disclosure of the information or content would be likely to be contrary to the public interest for any other reason."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "779412dbd136d56da858bb323950b36a1f10eb4e1e05ccf3d63842c4003ef2f7" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-allegiance-to-australia-act-2015-sch-1-sec-35a ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosure of certain information is prohibited in notices. Australian citizenship is a condition for the application of subsection (1)" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
